00:30:23.500 --> 00:30:25.750
able to send that event
to my Kubernetes cluster.

00:30:30.080 --> 00:30:34.150
So let's go ahead
and wrap this up.

00:30:34.150 --> 00:30:36.680
Why Cloud Run on Anthos?

00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:40.850
Well, easier deployment and
operations for microservices.

00:30:40.850 --> 00:30:41.810
I read a study--

00:30:41.810 --> 00:30:44.600
I can't remember where--
but it said around 25%,

00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:48.560
30% of your developers'
time is actually

00:30:48.560 --> 00:30:50.270
used doing non-developer work.

00:30:50.270 --> 00:30:53.450
So we hear the term "full
stack developer" a lot.

00:30:53.450 --> 00:30:56.990
So that usually means I'm
going to have to write YAML,

00:30:56.990 --> 00:30:59.300
I'm going to have
to manage nodes,

00:30:59.300 --> 00:31:02.210
I'm going to have
to set up databases.

00:31:02.210 --> 00:31:04.790
We make it easier for
you to use microservices

00:31:04.790 --> 00:31:08.300
by abstracting away a
lot of that operator work

00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:10.640
for the developers
to deploy, and then

00:31:10.640 --> 00:31:12.350
also make it easier
for the operators

00:31:12.350 --> 00:31:14.120
to work on the stuff
they need to work on,

00:31:14.120 --> 00:31:18.890
and not necessarily need to be
a part of the deployment process

00:31:18.890 --> 00:31:21.542
when an application version
needs to be deployed.

00:31:21.542 --> 00:31:23.000
Because of that,
you have increased

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:24.140
productivity and velocity.

00:31:24.140 --> 00:31:26.930
Hey, those developers get
that 25%, 30% of their time

00:31:26.930 --> 00:31:30.590
back to actually
develop applications.

00:31:30.590 --> 00:31:32.570
And of course, the
end of the story

00:31:32.570 --> 00:31:35.000
is that it enables your
developers and operators

00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:40.300
to be more successful and focus
on the things that matter.

00:31:40.300 --> 00:31:41.720
And thank you.

00:31:41.720 --> 00:31:44.210
And here's how you get Cloud
Run, and all of our code

00:31:44.210 --> 00:31:46.580
is in these repos,
and get some tips.

00:31:46.580 --> 00:31:49.270
And yeah, thank
you for the time.

00:31:49.270 --> 00:31:51.720
[APPLAUSE]

